  "finalText": "I've put Dana Whitfield's new address on O-1001, the order that hadn't gone out. The order in transit, O-1002, is unchanged.\n\n**O-1001 (not yet shipped):** the shipping address changed from 12 Alder Lane, Bristol BS1 4TR, UK to **7 Quarry Rise, Sheffield S11 8XZ, UK**. Before changing it I checked that the order and both its lines were still `pending` with no ship date. Reading the order again afterwards showed the new address, and nothing else had changed:\n- It is still `pending`.\n- It still has the same two lines: L1 (one P-KEY) and L2 (two P-CAB).\n- It shows 16700¢ paid and nothing refunded.\n\n**O-1002 (in transit):** I made no changes. It shipped on 2026-07-07, and store rules say a shipped order's address must never change because the shipping record has to stay accurate. Reading it again afterwards showed it still going to **88 Old Mill Road, Bristol BS3 2QQ, UK**, still `shipped` with the same 2026-07-07 ship date, and nothing refunded.\n\nYou may want to tell Dana that O-1002 is still on its way to 88 Old Mill Road. If she can't receive it there, she'll need to ask the carrier to redirect it. That can't be done by changing the order.\n\nThere were no refunds, cancellations or stock changes, and I didn't touch her customer record. The store system's date is 2026-07-25 while today is 2026-10-05, but no time limit applies to an address change, so it made no difference.",
